From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
Date: Thu, 12 Nov 2026 06:53:42 +0000
Subject: media: cedrus: vp9: do not disable the engine when a context stops

All the contexts share the one video engine, and the m2m framework runs
the jobs of the other contexts while one of them stops streaming.
Writing VE_MODE_DISABLED from the VP9 stop callback could therefore
abort a picture another context was decoding, which then failed on the
watchdog. Every job enables the engine mode it needs in its setup, so
there is nothing to disable when a context stops.

Assisted-by: LLM
Signed-off-by: Arun Iyengar <aiyengar1990@gmail.com>
---
 drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp9.c | 2 --
 1 file changed, 2 deletions(-)

diff --git a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp9.c b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp9.c
index af8a24f8f..e2553ceb7 100644
--- a/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp9.c
+++ b/drivers/staging/media/sunxi/cedrus/cedrus_vp9.c
@@ -1412,8 +1412,6 @@ static void cedrus_vp9_stop(struct cedrus_ctx *ctx)
 	struct cedrus_dev *dev = ctx->dev;
 	struct cedrus_vp9_ctx *vp9 = cedrus_vp9_ctx(ctx);
 
-	cedrus_engine_disable(dev);
-
 	dma_free_coherent(dev->dev, vp9->col_mv_buf_size,
 			  vp9->col_mv_buf, vp9->col_mv_buf_dma);
 	dma_free_coherent(dev->dev, CEDRUS_VP9_NEIGHBOR_BUF_SIZE,
-- 
